# Security headers for myfax.pages.dev — Doctrine §16.6
#
# The CSP is real, not aspirational: index.html carries no inline script and
# no inline style (styles live in styles.css; the version and release notes
# are classic script FILES), so 'self' holds for both. connect-src is https:
# because the relay address is the reader's own configured Worker URL — any
# https origin they choose — and the app must be able to reach it.
#
# No Strict-Transport-Security: pages.dev is HTTPS-only and Cloudflare owns
# TLS for it; a lock-in header that cannot be tested from here would be worse
# than leaving it to the platform.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src https:; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
